 RUN SETTINGS
 ------------
 Deck:               /home/peter/Dropbox/Research_Leuven/MarXus/validation/ZZAllyl+O2_Gamma_Case2/marxus_input/case2_tstlevel_E.inp
 Method:             STEADY STATE, OLZMANN (final steady state; steady-state family)
                     J N = R F without an absorbing barrier (Gonzalez-Garcia, Olzmann, PCCP 12, 12290 (2010), eqs. 7, 8)
                     with the thermal rate coefficients of the lowest eigenpair of the same J (eq. 12)
                     and the thermal fates of the wells (Boltzmann distribution of one well as source)
 Solvers:            linear systems: banded Cholesky factorization of the symmetrized J, relative residual <= 1e-8
                     thermal eigenpair: InverseIteration, sum-rule tolerance 1.5e-2 (warning only)
 Parallel:           4 cores (--ncore); the 21 conditions (T, p) in batches of 4 at a time (rayon)
                     BLAS threads per LAPACK call: 1
 Temperatures (K):   270, 280, 290, 300, 310, 320, 330
 Pressures (torr):   500, 600, 760
 Energy grid:        grains of 38.000 cm-1 on a common absolute scale, sums of 1 cm-1 counting cells
 Collisions:         exponential down, exactly normalized (Robertson (ed.), CCK 43 (2019), eq. 4.16), transitions up to 15 <dE_down>
                     low-energy reservoirs where eq. 4.16 fails (sparse states, Robertson 2019, p. 294): the grains from the
                       failing one down form one thermalized state (reservoir state, MESMER manual, Sec. 14.2.1):
                       T = 270 K: G2 6 grains (228 cm-1, 20.7 k_BT below the lowest threshold), G3 6 grains (228 cm-1, 31.0 k_BT below the lowest threshold), G4 5 grains (190 cm-1, 26.5 k_BT below the lowest threshold), G6 4 grains (152 cm-1, 27.1 k_BT below the lowest threshold)
                       T = 280 K: G2 6 grains (228 cm-1, 19.9 k_BT below the lowest threshold), G3 7 grains (266 cm-1, 29.7 k_BT below the lowest threshold), G4 6 grains (228 cm-1, 25.4 k_BT below the lowest threshold), G6 4 grains (152 cm-1, 26.2 k_BT below the lowest threshold)
                       T = 290 K: G2 7 grains (266 cm-1, 19.0 k_BT below the lowest threshold), G3 7 grains (266 cm-1, 28.7 k_BT below the lowest threshold), G4 6 grains (228 cm-1, 24.5 k_BT below the lowest threshold), G6 4 grains (152 cm-1, 25.3 k_BT below the lowest threshold)
                       T = 300 K: G2 8 grains (304 cm-1, 18.2 k_BT below the lowest threshold), G3 8 grains (304 cm-1, 27.5 k_BT below the lowest threshold), G4 6 grains (228 cm-1, 23.7 k_BT below the lowest threshold), G6 5 grains (190 cm-1, 24.2 k_BT below the lowest threshold)
                       T = 310 K: G2 9 grains (342 cm-1, 17.5 k_BT below the lowest threshold), G3 8 grains (304 cm-1, 26.6 k_BT below the lowest threshold), G4 8 grains (304 cm-1, 22.6 k_BT below the lowest threshold), G6 7 grains (266 cm-1, 23.1 k_BT below the lowest threshold)
                       T = 320 K: G2 9 grains (342 cm-1, 16.9 k_BT below the lowest threshold), G3 9 grains (342 cm-1, 25.6 k_BT below the lowest threshold), G4 8 grains (304 cm-1, 21.9 k_BT below the lowest threshold), G6 7 grains (266 cm-1, 22.4 k_BT below the lowest threshold)
                       T = 330 K: G2 10 grains (380 cm-1, 16.2 k_BT below the lowest threshold), G3 10 grains (380 cm-1, 24.7 k_BT below the lowest threshold), G4 9 grains (342 cm-1, 21.0 k_BT below the lowest threshold), G6 8 grains (304 cm-1, 21.5 k_BT below the lowest threshold)
                     collision frequency: Lennard-Jones (per well, below); collision integral Omega(2,2)*: Neufeld, Janzen, Aziz, J. Chem. Phys. 57, 1100 (1972) (default)
 Tunneling:          exact Eckart transmission (Miller, J. Am. Chem. Soc. 101, 6810 (1979), eq. 8)
 Source:             thermal reactant R through B12 (R -> G2)
                     F(E) ~ rho(E) k(E) exp(-E/kT) of the entrance channels (Pfeifle, Olzmann, IJCK 46, 231 (2014), eqs. 7, 9)
